<title>FRANCE: AGF to sell SAFR stake to Swiss Re.</title>
<headline>AGF to sell SAFR stake to Swiss Re.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-02-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>French insurer AGF said on Wednesday it signed a definitive accord to sell its 47 percent stake in Societe Anonyme Francaise de Reassurances (SAFR) for 2.5 billion French francs to Swiss Re.</p>
<p>AGF said that Worms &amp; Cie unit Athena joined in the agreement and sold its 10 percent stake in SAFR to Swiss Re for 1,470 francs per share, the same terms as AGF.</p>
<p>The deal values SAFR at 5.49 billion francs and will allow AGF to record a capital gain of some 970 million francs on the sale, AGF said.</p>
<p>As part of the deal AGF will acquire from Swiss Re 14 percent of credit insurer EULER for 756 million francs.</p>
</text>
